{"description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "Ben Franklin loved to swim and, at the age of eleven, he was determined to swim like a fish--fins and all! This account of young Ben's earliest invention follows the budding scientist's journey as he tests and retests his swim fins."}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2020-08-30T02:28:55.085697"}, "title": "Ben Franklin's big splash", "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2019-07-18T14:15:20.906262"}, "covers": [9323745], "subjects": ["Fiction", "Juvenile fiction", "Inventors", "Inventions", "Swimming", "Franklin, benjamin, 1706-1790", "Franklin, benjamin, 1706-1790, juvenile literature", "Inventors, juvenile literature"], "subject_people": ["Benjamin Franklin (1706-1790)"], "key": "/works/OL19983529W", "authors": [{"type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}, "author": {"key": "/authors/OL7237809A"}}], "latest_revision": 3, "type": {"key": "/type/work"}, "revision": 3}